<h1>balance</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The (weight) balance of a tree is the number of <a href="leaf.html"><em>leaves</em></a> of the left subtree of a tree, denoted |T<sub>l</sub>|, divided by the total number of leaves of the tree.  Formally, &rho;(T)  = |T<sub>l</sub>|/|T|.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> root balance.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bbalphatree.html"><em>BB(&alpha;) tree</em></a>, <a href="heightBalancedTree.html"><em>height-balanced tree</em></a>, <a href="rightrotatn.html"><em>right rotation</em></a>, <a href="leftrotation.html"><em>left rotation</em></a>, <a href="relaxedBalance.html"><em>relaxed balance</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The balance of a node is the balance of the (sub)tree rooted at that node. After <strong>Johann Blieberger</strong> &lt;<a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="6b0907020e092b0a1e1f04451f1e1c020e05450a08450a1f">[email&#160;protected]</a>&gt;, <em>Discrete Loops and Worst Case Performance</em>, page 22.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

